            <ArticleTitle>Incidence of penile pain after injection of a new formulation of prostaglandin E1.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We determined the incidence of pain with injection of a new formulation of prostaglandin E1.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A total of 63 subjects with erectile dysfunction underwent treatment with the new formulation of prostaglandin E1. Evidence of pain associated with injection was obtained by questionnaire and through questioning.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A total of 451 injections was given to 63 subjects in the office, with 16 episodes (3.5%) of pain in 10 (15.9%). Then, 680 injections were performed by 38 subjects at home, with 15 episodes (2.2%) of pain in 8 (21%). Pain was not dose related.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The new formulation of prostaglandin E1 is less likely to be associated with pain compared with alcohol based formulations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
